{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-09-18T21:33:59.885Z","data":{"text":"Task 4 is complete. Summary:\n\n## What was built\n\n**`src/core/doctor.ts`** (198 lines) — `runDoctorChecks(projectRoot, deps?)` returns a `DoctorReport` with five checks in order:\n- `config` — loads config in a try/catch and validates required properties\n- `harness` — resolves the configured binary and probes `<bin> --version` (mock needs none)\n- `managed-blocks` — validates `PLANNER.md` strictly; tolerates an unmanaged `AGENTS.md`\n- `locks` — scans `openspec/changes` + legacy `specs/` for `.run/running/*.pid` with dead PIDs\n- `archives` — validates each archived change has `proposal.md`/`spec.md` + `tasks/`/`tasks.md`\n\n**`src/cli/doctor.ts`** (33 lines) — prints `[ok]`/`[fail] <name>: <message>` per check and sets exit code 1 on any failure.\n\n**`src/cli/index.ts`** — registers the `doctor` command.\n\n**`tests/doctor.test.ts`** (259 lines) — 12 tests covering all checks, CLI output/exit, and a binary-gated run against the active checkout.\n\n## Verification\n- `node --import tsx --test tests/doctor.test.ts` → 12 pass, 0 fail, exit 0\n- `osq doctor` on the active checkout → 5 `[ok]` lines, exit 0\n- `pnpm tsc --noEmit` clean, `pnpm lint` clean\n- Full suite: 513 pass / 1 fail (pre-existing out-of-scope `tests/harness.test.ts` from task 2)\n\n## Key deviation (documented in `.run/results/4.md`)\nThe active checkout's hand-authored `AGENTS.md` has no osq markers and is out of scope, making the literal \"both files must have markers\" rule incompatible with acceptance line 15. Doctor treats a markerless `AGENTS.md` as unmanaged while still failing on partial/reversed markers and a markerless `PLANNER.md`. The harness check also uses a direct `--version` probe rather than the adapter `preflight`, since core cannot import harness and `preflightOpencode` calls `process.exit`."}}
